# Falkensteinwand back wall (decorative, NON-solid, like wall_village_bg;
# D-038): the shaft's back wall and the Einsiedelei cave interior. The same
# quiet stratum as kalkfels in shadow: m body, one wavy d bedding line and
# a short d joint; no light lip, no grass. Edges are recessed, never lit: an
# open top gets a 2 px ragged d shadow whose row 0 has 1-2 px transparent
# notches every 2-4 px, an open left a ragged d shadow column; open right
# and bottom stay flat. The top counts as joined under any drawn tile (rock,
# plank, box, brick; D-063), so the top shadow and notches show only
# against air/sky above. Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_kalkfels_bg
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
---
frame auto 0
